# --- Rust/Cargo ---
/src-rust/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# `Cargo.lock` is **committed**, not ignored. This crate ships a [[bin]], and
# the package build, the container image and the release workflow all build
# from a clean checkout — so without it every one of them re-resolves
# dependencies from scratch and a semver-compatible upstream release can break
# a build with no change here and nothing in git to bisect. `PKGBUILD` already
# passes `--locked`, which fails outright on a fresh clone if the lock file is
# not there.

# --- Node/Frontend ---
node_modules/
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store

# The SPA is embedded at compile time, so `dist/` must exist before any cargo
# command. Excluding the directory outright would make that a permanent
# "run npm first" exception — and git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so the exclusion is on the contents and .gitkeep is
# committed. A build without `npm run build` then serves a 404 at `/`: a loud
# runtime failure instead of a confusing build failure.
dist/*
!dist/.gitkeep

# --- Log files ---
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- Editor Specific ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Generated architecture docs (sysyviz output) ---
docs/arch/
